 "closes": true,
 "closes_note": "ALL FIFTEEN FOOTED COLUMNS CLOSE EXACTLY - seven of seven in the male block, eight of eight in the female block, 175 people. Three marks were refused and are named rather than buried: the long sweeping stroke standing in the male under-5 cell of line 2, and the two lighter marks in the same column on lines 23 and 30, all three of which lie on the path of the flourished tails this hand gives the names to their left and none of which is a numeral form; and one mark in the female 20-30 cell of line 5, which a gridded re-read at 2.2x showed to be the descender of the 2 written above it on line 4. Each refusal was made on the page. The male under-5 column foots 10 with them out and would foot 13 with the first three in.",
